Andrea is currently the Chief Operating Officer for Girl Scouts of Hawaiʻi, where she develops and executes strategic plans to empower over 1,800 Girl Scouts across the state.
Previously, as Acting CEO of Hawaiian Building Maintenance, she led the state’s largest maintenance and janitorial company with more than 600 employees across four islands. 
Prior to entering the private sector, Andrea built a distinguished career as a U.S. Navy Submarine Warfare officer, serving in high-stakes operational and strategic roles, including at The White House as Senior Watch Officer of the President’s Emergency Operations Center directly supporting the President and Vice President. In her Navy career, she served on three submarines, including as the senior woman integrating the submarine’s crew as a Department Head. 
Andrea has advanced degrees in Security Studies (Georgetown University) and Mechanical Engineering (Columbia University), as well as published research in operations and systems optimization.
Andrea and her husband, Rick Smith, reside in Kāneʻohe and are devoted parents to their three children. Andrea is a classical harpist with significant experience performing as a soloist and in ensembles.

